From: SBE1V1K build <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: qualcommbe: keep the in-kernel QCA8081 driver, drop only the QCA8084 registration

6.12 的 qualcommbe 目标配置打开了 CONFIG_QCA808X_PHY=y，内核里因此编进
drivers/net/phy/qcom/qca808x.c。原 0030 的修法是把这个配置整个关掉，用来
躲开 libphy 驱动名 "Qualcomm QCA8084" 与 QSDK kmod-qca8084 的 EEXIST
（-16）冲突；代价是 QCA8081 也失去厂商驱动，落到 genphy。

2026-11-19 真机对照实验（本机 USB RTL8156B 直连 eth1，dnsmasq 做 DHCP）：

  - 对端 2500 Mb/s：链路 up，但 25 s 抓包零帧、5 s 计数增量 0、
    ping 100% 丢包、neigh INCOMPLETE（完全静默）；
  - 同一条线降到 1000F：DHCP 成功、ping 3/3、REACHABLE（全通）；
  - 换成 24.10-6.6 的 A 机（QCA8081 厂商驱动在位）：2500 下主动发
    DHCP DISCOVER、拿到租约、ping 3/3、全通。

结论：genphy 不会把 MAC/PCS 切到 PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_2500BASEX，也缺
SGMII FIFO / 主从处理——2.5G 链路"假通"。新的修法：保留
CONFIG_QCA808X_PHY=y，只用内核补丁 0801 去掉 qca808x.c 里 QCA8084 那一条
phy_driver 注册，QCA8084 依旧由 QSDK qca8084-phy.ko 负责，QCA8081 用回
厂商驱动。四个失去引用的 QCA8084 入口函数标 __maybe_unused（目标开
CONFIG_WERROR=y，未用静态函数会直接编译失败）。

本补丁以新增内核补丁文件的形式落地：

diff -ruN a/target/linux/qualcommbe/patches-6.12/0801-qca808x-drop-qca8084-driver.patch b/target/linux/qualcommbe/patches-6.12/0801-qca808x-drop-qca8084-driver.patch
diff -ruN a/target/linux/qualcommbe/patches-6.12/0801-qca808x-drop-qca8084-driver.patch b/target/linux/qualcommbe/patches-6.12/0801-qca808x-drop-qca8084-driver.patch
--- a/target/linux/qualcommbe/patches-6.12/0801-qca808x-drop-qca8084-driver.patch	1970-01-01 00:00:00.000000000 +0000
+++ b/target/linux/qualcommbe/patches-6.12/0801-qca808x-drop-qca8084-driver.patch	2026-11-19 13:57:53.094254525 +0000
@@ -0,0 +1,93 @@
+From: SBE1V1K build <noreply@example.invalid>
+Subject: [PATCH] net: phy: qca808x: keep the QCA8081 driver, drop the QCA8084 registration
+
+qualcommbe builds drivers/net/phy/qcom/qca808x.c with
+CONFIG_QCA808X_PHY=y.  The file registers both the QCA8081 and the
+"Qualcomm QCA8084" libphy drivers.  The SBE1V1K image also loads the
+QSDK qca8084-phy.ko, whose driver registers the same name; libphy
+answers EEXIST (-16) and the kmodloader chain qca8084-phy -> qca-ssdk
+-> qca-nss-ppe -> qca-nss-dp/sfe/ecm dies, so the board boots without
+any Ethernet port (documented in 25.12-6.12/patches/0030).
+
+Disabling CONFIG_QCA808X_PHY entirely avoids the clash but also drops
+the QCA8081 vendor driver and leaves eth1 (QCA8081, 2.5G WAN) on
+genphy.  genphy never switches the MAC/PCS to PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_2500BASEX
+and lacks the SGMII FIFO and master/slave handling, so at 2.5G the link
+reports up but carries zero frames.  2026-11-19 A/B experiment with a
+known-good 2.5G partner: 24.10 (vendor driver) is fully bidirectional at
+2500 Mb/s, while 25.12 (genphy) is silent at 2500 but fully working at
+1000 Mb/s.
+
+The QCA8084 PHY is owned by the QSDK module on this board, so drop only
+the QCA8084 element from qca808x_driver[] and keep the QCA8081 driver.
+The four now-unreferenced QCA8084 entry points are marked __maybe_unused
+because the target builds with CONFIG_WERROR=y.
+
+--- a/drivers/net/phy/qcom/qca808x.c	2026-11-19 13:55:57.015891603 +0000
++++ b/drivers/net/phy/qcom/qca808x.c	2026-11-19 13:57:46.247636487 +0000
+@@ -940,7 +940,7 @@
+ 	return qca8084_package_clock_init(shared_priv);
+ }
+ 
+-static int qca8084_config_init(struct phy_device *phydev)
++static int __maybe_unused qca8084_config_init(struct phy_device *phydev)
+ {
+ 	int ret;
+ 
+@@ -974,7 +974,7 @@
+ 			     QCA8084_MSE_THRESHOLD_2P5G_VAL);
+ }
+ 
+-static void qca8084_link_change_notify(struct phy_device *phydev)
++static void __maybe_unused qca8084_link_change_notify(struct phy_device *phydev)
+ {
+ 	struct qca808x_shared_priv *shared_priv;
+ 	int ret;
+@@ -1142,7 +1142,7 @@
+ 					    shared_priv->mdiodev[0]);
+ }
+ 
+-static int qca8084_probe(struct phy_device *phydev)
++static int __maybe_unused qca8084_probe(struct phy_device *phydev)
+ {
+ 	struct qca808x_shared_priv *shared_priv;
+ 	struct device *dev = &phydev->mdio.dev;
+@@ -1181,7 +1181,7 @@
+ 	return reset_control_deassert(rstc);
+ }
+ 
+-static void qca8084_remove(struct phy_device *phydev)
++static void __maybe_unused qca8084_remove(struct phy_device *phydev)
+ {
+ 	if (phydev->interface != PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_10G_QXGMII)
+ 		return;
+@@ -1219,29 +1219,6 @@
+ 	.led_hw_control_set	= qca808x_led_hw_control_set,
+ 	.led_hw_control_get	= qca808x_led_hw_control_get,
+ 	.led_polarity_set	= qca808x_led_polarity_set,
+-}, {
+-	/* Qualcomm QCA8084 */
+-	PHY_ID_MATCH_MODEL(QCA8084_PHY_ID),
+-	.name			= "Qualcomm QCA8084",
+-	.flags			= PHY_POLL_CABLE_TEST,
+-	.config_intr		= at803x_config_intr,
+-	.handle_interrupt	= at803x_handle_interrupt,
+-	.get_tunable		= at803x_get_tunable,
+-	.set_tunable		= at803x_set_tunable,
+-	.set_wol		= at803x_set_wol,
+-	.get_wol		= at803x_get_wol,
+-	.get_features		= qca808x_get_features,
+-	.config_aneg		= qca808x_config_aneg,
+-	.suspend		= genphy_suspend,
+-	.resume			= genphy_resume,
+-	.read_status		= qca808x_read_status,
+-	.soft_reset		= qca808x_soft_reset,
+-	.cable_test_start	= qca808x_cable_test_start,
+-	.cable_test_get_status	= qca808x_cable_test_get_status,
+-	.config_init		= qca8084_config_init,
+-	.link_change_notify	= qca8084_link_change_notify,
+-	.probe			= qca8084_probe,
+-	.remove			= qca8084_remove,
+ }, };
+ 
+ module_phy_driver(qca808x_driver);
